infographic hierarchy-tree-curved-line-rounded-rect-node
data
  title Three ways to invalidate — no free option
  desc Each trades the same two axes (staleness vs coupling) and carries its own signature failure mode
  root
    label Cache invalidation
    children
      - label TTL expiry
        desc Write path does nothing; cache self-heals. Simple and decoupled, but bounded staleness — a value can be wrong up to the TTL.
      - label Explicit delete
        desc Delete the key on every write; staleness near zero. But the write path is coupled to every derived key, and a missed site stays stale forever — plus the write-time delete race.
      - label Versioned keys
        desc Bump the version per write (v7 to v8); race-free since you never mutate a shared key. Cost: orphaned old versions to evict and a version source to track.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e #14b8a6
